 "about": "The reach map as a table of answers, shared by every reader of reach-map-4ace.json: the page guard (sdk/js/examples/twin/reach-guard.js) and the Python reference (tools/reach/query.py) must give these answers, and so must the body when it reads a map (#7513). Poses are in the MAP's counts (shoulder, elbow, pitch; pitch up is fewer counts). safe = the pose itself is a safe grid pose; ranges_shrink_N = [low, high] counts the joint may go to with the others held, the run of safe grid poses holding the pose, N counts in from each end and never past the pose itself; null = the pose is not safe, so no range. Frame cases: a lamp's counts minus frame.offset are the map's counts. Made from the page guard; the Python test is the independent check. restrict_cases / restrict_all_cases: the page guard's answer to a goal in DEGREES (the page's unit: shoulder and elbow from folded, pitch up positive; the pose is where the lamp is and its goal), at the 48-count margin: deg = what is sent, kind = null (sent as asked), held_at_edge (a goal past the safe run is held at its inside edge) or refused_further (from a pose the map calls unsafe a goal no nearer safe is not sent: the lamp stays where it is); a goal toward safe is allowed. These move the lamp: the body's reader must give them.",
